component "the agent exits" as EXIT <<app>>
component "the ""teardown"" value\n""teardownPlan(failed)""" as PLAN <<app>>
component "a stop\nCtrl+C twice · SIGTERM · SIGHUP" as STOP <<host>>
component "the first Ctrl+C\nsays the step and what leaving keeps" as ONCE <<host>>
component """step(name, fn)""\nname · duration · outcome" as STEP <<app>>
database "the run log\n""step: clone/snapshot 1.2s ok""" as LOG <<db>>
component "four guest or network calls\nunder ""guestExecDeadline"" (3m)" as BOUND <<app>>
component "**a wedged sbx daemon**\nhung teardown before the carry" as HANG <<error>>
component "the rescue line\n""sbx ls"", then ""sbx rm --force""" as RESCUE <<host>>
component "the terminal\n""step 6/9 · clone/snapshot · 12s""" as TERM <<host>>

EXIT ARROW_MAIN PLAN : before Run's result
PLAN ARROW_MAIN STEP : each step, in plan order
ONCE ARROW_OPTIONAL STOP : pressed again
STOP ARROW_OPTIONAL PLAN : later steps are skipped
STOP ARROW_OPTIONAL BOUND : the call in flight ends
STEP ARROW_MAIN LOG : one row per step
PLAN ARROW_OPTIONAL TERM : one live line per step
STEP ARROW_MAIN BOUND
HANG ARROW_ERROR BOUND : what the deadline ends
BOUND ARROW_OPTIONAL RESCUE : a removal that timed out

note top of PLAN
  **A plan, not a closure.** The step names
  are a list a test can compare a run against.
  A panic in one step becomes that step's
  error, and the next step still runs.
end note

note top of STOP
  **A stopped teardown never removes.** The
  sandbox stays with its ide block, the steps
  not run are named, and proveo exits 130 for
  Ctrl+C or 128+signal for SIGTERM and SIGHUP.
end note

note top of ONCE
  **Say once, leave on two.** The calls in
  flight sit in their own process group, so
  the terminal's Ctrl+C reaches proveo alone
  and the first press costs nothing.
end note

note bottom of TERM
  **One line, with a clock.** The running step
  shows its place, its elapsed time and its
  ceiling, redrawn each second and erased when
  it ends. A pipe gets a start line instead.
end note

note bottom of LOG
  **The row goes to the log only.** It is for
  the next person reading a slow run. The
  screen gets the start line now and a live
  step list later, from the same names.
end note

note bottom of STEP
  **A parent and its parts.** ""clone"" is the
  whole carry; ""clone/snapshot"" is one part.
  Probes between parts count toward the
  parent, so the rows stay few.
end note

note bottom of HANG
  **It ran first, and unbounded.** The reflog
  read sits before the carry. With no deadline
  a wedged daemon stopped teardown silently,
  with the agent's work still in the sandbox.
end note

note bottom of RESCUE
  **Look before removing again.** A removal
  that hit its deadline may be half-done. The
  line names ""sbx ls"" first; proveo never
  kills the shim itself.
end note
@enduml
